# Node build inputs/outputs — installed and produced inside the image's Node
# stage, never sent from the host. Excluding the built assets here guarantees
# the Go stage embeds only what the Node stage produced, never a stale local copy.
#
# The ** matters. Docker matches these patterns against paths relative to the
# context root, so a bare `node_modules/` catches only a top-level one, and every
# npm workspace under web/ keeps its own. scripts/build-assets.sh runs `npm ci`
# in each of them inside the image, so the host copies are replaced even when
# they are sent.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
internal/api/assets/

# Local dev artifacts and data — not needed to build the image.
bin/
server
data/
*.db
.dolt/
.beads-credential-key
.git/

# Not build inputs. Nothing embeds from any of these: the only go:embed outside
# internal/api's assets, templates and migrations is internal/agent's
# ext/exhibit.ts. The root markdown and LICENSE stay, being small and the first
# thing anyone looks for.
.tickets/
docs/
design_files/
dev/
.github/

# Editor and platform cruft.
**/.DS_Store
